import lib/process.dl

function {process wait result:status} has no completion report:
    replacement:
        the inverse of (status reports completion)

function {process wait result:status} has no termination report:
    replacement:
        the inverse of (status reports termination)

function the live process test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set command to a process command for the live process test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import sys\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n sys.stdout.write('out:' + line); sys.stdout.flush()\n sys.stderr.write('err:' + line); sys.stderr.flush()" as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it

print whether child was launched as a line
poll child and set pending to it
print whether pending succeeded as a line
print whether pending has no completion report as a line
read the available standard output of child and set initial to it
print whether initial succeeded as a line
print whether (initial's contents = "") as a line
print whether initial has not reached the end of stream as a line

write (the string form of "first\n") to the standard input of child and set request to it
print whether request succeeded as a line
print request's byte count as a line
read the standard output of child and set response to it
read the standard error of child and set warning to it
print whether response succeeded as a line
print whether (response's contents = "out:first\n") as a line
print whether warning succeeded as a line
print whether (warning's contents = "err:first\n") as a line

write (the string form of "second\n") to the standard input of child and set followup to it
close the standard input of child and set closure to it
print whether followup succeeded as a line
print whether closure succeeded as a line
read the standard output of child and set following to it
read the standard error of child and set failure to it
print whether (following's contents = "out:second\n") as a line
print whether (failure's contents = "err:second\n") as a line

wait for child and set status to it
print whether status succeeded as a line
print whether status reports completion as a line
print status's exit code as a line
print whether status has no termination report as a line

set delay to a process command for the live process test interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to delay
add "import time; time.sleep(30)" as an argument to delay
launch delay and set sleeper to it
terminate sleeper and set termination to it
wait for sleeper and set terminated to it
print whether sleeper was launched as a line
print whether termination succeeded as a line
print whether terminated succeeded as a line
print whether terminated reports completion as a line
print whether terminated reports termination as a line

launch delay and set orphan to it
clean up orphan and set cleanup to it
print whether orphan was launched as a line
print whether cleanup succeeded as a line
